# Link follow-up work to its origin

When **implementation or testing** (also review/acceptance) exposes extra work,
file it in the vault **before it stays only in chat**. This includes bugs,
regressions, polish, chores, research, and newly discovered requirements.

| Discovery | Destination |
| --- | --- |
| Broken behavior / regression | `vault/production/bugs/` (`type: bug`, `status: Open`) |
| New/changed requirement or extra feature | `vault/production/tasks/` (`type: task`, `status: Not started`) |

Then:

1. Find the sprint note with `current: true`.
2. Set the item's `sprint` frontmatter to that sprint's short label (`Sprint N`).
3. Add `Origin: [[source task or bug]]` to the new item's body.
4. Add `Follow-up: [[new item]]` to the source item's body so navigation is
   bidirectional.
5. If there is no source item, link `Origin` to the current sprint note and
   briefly identify the review, test, acceptance pass, or chat request.
6. Deduplicate before creating; update existing links instead of cloning notes.
7. On the **source card**, add `Bugs found:` / `Follow-up:` and a **Resolution** section when that card is closed.

Examples: height-mismatch test reveals a second event never fires → bug.
Snapshot work needs a `why_not` field the card did not include → follow-up task.

Do not pull unrelated backlog ideas into the current sprint. Skip only tiny
edits inside the same open card ("rename this var") or an explicit
"не заводи задачу".
